knowledge:
- key_parameters:
    - lambda=Mixing parameter in [0,1] determining spatial information weight. Use lambda=0.2 for cell-typing and lambda=0.8 for domain/zone-finding (except Visium v1/v2 where lambda=0.2 is recommended for domain finding) ;;
    - k_geom=Number of spatial neighbors. Use k_geom=18 (or c(18, 18) if compute_agf=TRUE) for Visium v1/v2, k_geom=30 for STARmap PLUS, and custom values like c(15, 30) for multi-scale neighborhood analysis ;;
    - compute_agf=Logical; if TRUE, computes both the weighted neighborhood mean (H_0) and the azimuthal Gabor filter (H_1) to estimate gene expression gradients ;;
    - group=Grouping variable in colData (e.g., "sample_id") used during multi-sample runBanksyPCA to z-scale features separately per sample ;;
    - resolution=Resolution parameter for clustering (e.g., Leiden) ;;
    - k_neighbors=Number of nearest neighbors used to construct the shared nearest neighbors graph in clusterBanksy
- alternatives:
    - scrapper::computeRnaQcMetrics=Preferred over deprecated scuttle::perCellQCMetrics for quality control ;;
    - scrapper::centerSizeFactors=Preferred over deprecated scuttle::librarySizeFactors for normalization ;;
    - scrapper::normalizeCounts=Preferred over deprecated scuttle::normalizeCounts for log-normalization ;;
    - harmony::RunHarmony=Used on the BANKSY PCA embedding to integrate multiple spatial datasets and correct for batch effects
- when_to_use: Use when performing spatially-informed cell-typing or spatial domain segmentation on spatial transcriptomics datasets (e.g., 10x Visium, STARmap PLUS, VeraFISH).
- pitfalls:
    - Using default domain segmentation parameters (lambda=0.8, k_geom=30) on Visium v1/v2 datasets instead of the recommended lambda=0.2 and k_geom=18 ;;
    - Forgetting to stagger spatial coordinates when merging multiple samples, which can lead to spatial coordinate overlap ;;
    - Relying on deprecated scuttle functions (perCellQCMetrics, librarySizeFactors, normalizeCounts) instead of their scrapper equivalents
